WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.299
On November 28th, Nancy Pelosi cleared a
major hurdle in her quest to become

00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:13.500
Speaker of the House for the second time.
What do all Americans think about her

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.970
and what about Democrats? In November,
Gallup reported that Pelosi has long

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.260
been viewed more negatively than positively.
In the organization's latest 2018 poll,

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:28.960
29% had a favorable opinion
of her and 53% an unfavorable one.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.420
Should she be speaker again when the
party takes control in January?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.380
In the mid-November CBS News poll, 30%
nationally said that they would prefer Pelosi

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:44.460
to be the next speaker and 57% another
Democrat. 49% of Democrats preferred her

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.840
and 40% another Democrat. In a late
November Harvard-Harris online survey,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.720
33% nationally said that the House
should reelect her, while 67% said it was

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:02.540
time for a new leader. Democrats preferred
a new leader by a slim margin, 52 to 48%.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.860
Pelosi is formidable, but it's clear there
is an appetite for change among Democrats.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.240
Should Nancy Pelosi be speaker for a second time?

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.960
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.410
to cover in 60 seconds and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.090
research and videos from AEI.

